<title>SWITZERLAND: Crossair reports higher profit, dividend.</title>
<headline>Crossair reports higher profit, dividend.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996</p>
<p>				   (million Sfr unless stated)</p>
<p> Net profit		     23.0		vs 17.5</p>
<p> Turnover			 738.3	     vs 464.8</p>
<p> Cash flow			81.5		vs 59.6</p>
<p> Dividend (percent)	   6 pct	     vs 5 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - Crossair AG is majority-owned by Swissair and is the regional airline subsidiary of the Swissair group. It noted in a statement that 1996 growth included completion of a takeover of Swissair 100-seat aircraft and short-haul operations from dissolved unit Balair/CTA.</p>
<p>Crossair said it would release more information on 1996 results at a news conference on April 10.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
